## Iron(II) hydroxide
component-iron-ii-hydroxide = Iron(II) hydroxide
    .genitive = iron(II) hydroxide
component-iron-ii-hydroxide-description-novice = A white but almost always greenish sludge. In air it slowly turns brown — into rust.
component-iron-ii-hydroxide-description-school = It forms when Fe²⁺ ions meet hydroxide ions: Fe²⁺ + 2OH⁻ → Fe(OH)₂↓. Oxygen from the air oxidises it to iron(III) compounds — brown rust.
component-iron-ii-hydroxide-model-notes = How the sludge browns in air (turns to rust) is not computed yet: it is shown greenish.
